  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (ignoring probabilities) and then comparing each lottery based on the probability of exceeding this level. The aspiration level (-1750) and the comparison of probabilities of positive deviations from it are central to the reason. However, the individual does not mention any such calculation or reference point. Instead, they describe a heuristic based on probability sensitivity when outcomes are similar, focusing on the 5 percentage point difference in favor of B (80% vs. 75%) and weighing it against the 1000 Euro worse loss. This suggests a probability-focused compensatory trade-off, but not one structured around deviations from an aspiration level derived from all outcomes. There is no evidence that the individual computed or used the mean of all outcomes as a reference. The justification is consistent with a probability dominance heuristic under similar outcomes, not with the aspiration-level rule defined. Therefore, while both the reason and the individual give weight to probabilities, the structure and basis of reasoning differ fundamentally.",
